          "a": "A static route to the null interface, e.g. ip route 200.5.16.0 255.255.240.0 Null0, creating 200.5.16.0/20 → Null0; it is commonly used in routing designs to prevent unwanted forwarding loops when a summary is advertised.",
          "tag": "Core Concept",
          "context": "Practical"
