          "q": "How does BPDU Guard relate to Root Guard, and can they be configured on the same port?",
          "a": "BPDU Guard protects edge ports. Root Guard protects root placement on segments facing other switches. They address different problems and generally apply to different types of ports; both can use the spanning-tree guard <keyword> form but the configuration context differs.",
