          "q": "Summarize the CEF quick review: structures, source, lookup, and load sharing.",
          "a": "CEF = Cisco Express Forwarding, Cisco's forwarding architecture, main purpose efficient packet forwarding, main structures FIB + adjacency information. FIB source is the RIB; FIB lookup is longest-prefix match; L2 rewrite comes from adjacency information. ECMP uses hash-based load sharing, commonly per-flow/per-destination, hash behavior platform-dependent; polarization is possible in multi-stage ECMP; recursive lookup is resolved before normal forwarding; main command is show ip cef.",
          "tag": "Quick Review",
