          "q": "Describe the classic tag-based loop-prevention workflow.",
          "a": "1) Tag OSPF routes entering EIGRP as 100; 2) On EIGRP-to-OSPF redistribution, deny tag 100; 3) Result: OSPF routes never bounce back into EIGRP, breaking the redistribution feedback loop deterministically.",
