      "cards": [
        {
          "q": "What is Layer 2 troubleshooting concerned with?",
          "a": "Switching: VLANs, trunks, MAC learning, STP, and ports. Problems appear as no MAC learned, VLAN missing, or STP blocking.",
          "tag": "Overview",
          "context": "Both"
        },
        {
          "q": "What is the Layer 2 verification order?",
          "a": "Link up, VLAN exists, port in VLAN, MAC learned, trunk carries VLAN, then STP state. Work up the switch database.",
          "tag": "Core Concept",
          "context": "Both"
        },
        {
          "q": "What command proves the switch sees hosts on a port?",
          "a": "show mac address-table, which shows learned MACs.",
          "tag": "Core Concept",
          "context": "Practical"
        },
        {
          "q": "What command shows the VLAN list on a switch?",
          "a": "show vlan (or show vlan brief).",
          "tag": "Core Concept",
          "context": "Practical"
        },
        {
          "q": "What command shows trunk information?",
          "a": "show interfaces trunk.",
          "tag": "Core Concept",
          "context": "Practical"
        },
        {
          "q": "What are the two top causes of Layer 2 issues?",
          "a": "VLAN mismatch and trunk filtering (allowed VLAN list).",
          "tag": "Core Concept",
          "context": "Exam"
        },
        {
          "q": "What silent failure does a native VLAN mismatch cause on a trunk?",
          "a": "Native VLAN mismatch causes silent loss of traffic between the two ends.",
          "tag": "Core Concept",
          "context": "Exam"
        },
        {
          "q": "What is the relationship between STP blocking and loops?",
          "a": "STP blocking is normal and expected; loops are the actual failure. Look for loops rather than treating a blocked port as an error.",
          "tag": "Exam Trap",
          "context": "Both"
        },
        {
          "q": "What should the trunk configuration be for encapsulation and mode?",
          "a": "Encapsulation 802.1Q and switchport mode trunk. Avold relying on VTP.",
          "tag": "Core Concept",
          "context": "Exam"
        },
        {
          "q": "What three tools resolve most Layer 2 issues?",
          "a": "The MAC table, show vlan, and show interfaces trunk.",
          "tag": "Core Concept",
          "context": "Practical"
        },
        {
          "q": "A broadcast storm on the network is most likely caused by what?",
          "a": "A loop in the network (unblocked STP or a switching loop).",
          "tag": "Core Concept",
          "context": "Exam"
        },
        {
          "q": "How do you confirm the VLAN a port belongs to?",
          "a": "Use show interfaces switchport or show interfaces status to verify the VLAN assignment.",
          "tag": "Core Concept",
          "context": "Practical"
        },
        {
          "q": "Why is an unknown MAC in the table a Layer 2 concern?",
          "a": "An unknown or wrong MAC can indicate a VLAN mismatch or a port assignment problem.",
          "tag": "Quick Review",
          "context": "Exam"
        }
      ]
